@startuml KTOB_09_sequence_recommendation
title KTOB — Recommendations with Consent and Boundaries
actor Reader
participant "Angular UI" as UI
participant "Java API" as API
participant "Privacy module" as Privacy
participant "Advisor module" as Advisor
database "Supabase Postgres" as DB
participant "AI provider" as AI
Reader -> UI : Request recommendations
UI -> API : recommend(mode, request, exceptions)
API -> Privacy : verify reader, read consent / boundaries
Privacy -> DB : fetch explicit restrictions
DB --> Privacy : opt-in, firm boundaries, permitted scopes
Privacy --> API : safe request policy
alt Explicit per-request exception
 API -> Privacy : validate reader authorized exception
 Privacy --> API : scoped exception
end
alt Personalization opted in
 API -> Advisor : build allowed reading context
 Advisor -> DB : retrieve only permitted books, notes, memories
 DB --> Advisor : filtered context
else Personalization off
 API -> Advisor : no private reading context
end
Advisor -> AI : request (permitted context or generic)
AI --> Advisor : suggestions and explanations
Advisor -> Privacy : enforce boundaries on candidates
alt Verified safe candidates
 Privacy --> Advisor : allowed recommendations
else Content safety uncertain or conflicting
 Privacy --> Advisor : reject / mark uncertainty
end
Advisor --> API : verified/qualified recommendations
API --> UI : suggestions + source/uncertainty explanations
UI --> Reader : view and give optional feedback
note over Privacy, Advisor
'SURPRISE ME' never silently bypasses firm boundaries.
Unknown warning data never proves a book safe.
end note
@enduml
